< # scan_to_scan_filter_chain config — angle-based body filter for /scan.
< #
< # Empirical calibration (sim, robot in obstacle-free area):
< #   - LIDAR: 360 samples over [-180°, +180°], range_min = 0.40 m
< #   - 53/360 points return body reflections (= 14.7% of the scan):
< #       * rear panel (-180° → -170° and +170° → +180°): ~0.72 m
< #       * side wings (-168° → -150° and +155° → +168°):  0.40–0.50 m
< #       * worst case body return at idx 30: angle = -149.92°
< #   → body angular footprint ≈ ±150° to ±180° (50° total at the rear)
< #
< # Optimal filter with 10° safety margin (covers vibration, calibration drift,
< # manufacturing tolerance, etc.):
< #   - keep angles in [-140°, +140°] = [-2.443 rad, +2.443 rad]
< #   - chops rear ±40° (80° total) — the upstream default chopped ±45° (90°),
< #     this recovers 5° on each side while still leaving a 10° margin from
< #     the worst measured body return.
< #
< # DO NOT raise these beyond ±149° in this URDF — at that point the filter
< # starts letting wing returns through and the obstacle guards in
< # `dock_trigger.py` will see the body as a permanent obstacle. Re-measure
< # if you change the LIDAR mount, robot chassis, or URDF.
